WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.001 --> 00:00:07.209
"Hormesis from Low-Dose Radiation"

00:00:07.325 --> 00:00:09.680
Hormesis was first
shown to extend life

00:00:09.680 --> 00:00:11.640
more than a century ago

00:00:11.640 --> 00:00:14.840
when low doses of radiation
were shown to increase

00:00:14.840 --> 00:00:17.400
the lifespan
of a type of beetle.

00:00:17.400 --> 00:00:19.680
Scientists were hoping
irradiation with x-rays

00:00:19.680 --> 00:00:22.520
could kill off the eggs
of the grain pest,

00:00:22.520 --> 00:00:24.120
but to their surprise,
at low doses,

00:00:24.120 --> 00:00:27.000
it actually made the beetles
live longer.

00:00:27.000 --> 00:00:29.520
This was subsequently
replicated with gamma rays,

00:00:29.520 --> 00:00:30.920
and in about
a dozen other insects

00:00:30.920 --> 00:00:33.560
from house flies and crickets
to wasps and mosquitoes:

00:00:33.560 --> 00:00:38.960
a strongly consistent 20 to 60
percent increase in lifespan.

00:00:38.960 --> 00:00:41.000
What is going on?

00:00:41.000 --> 00:00:44.000
Hormesis is thought to be
an adaptive response

00:00:44.000 --> 00:00:46.680
to anticipated
potential threats.

00:00:46.680 --> 00:00:49.800
The body is able
to leverage the initial insult

00:00:49.800 --> 00:00:52.680
to prompt a compensatory
counter response

00:00:52.680 --> 00:00:55.320
that more than covers
the cost of the original damage

00:00:55.320 --> 00:00:58.680
and yields a net benefit
in the end.

00:00:58.680 --> 00:01:01.200
In the case of radiation,
at high enough doses,

00:01:01.200 --> 00:01:03.960
it kills by damaging DNA.

00:01:03.960 --> 00:01:07.240
Animals have a whole
DNA repair apparatus,

00:01:07.240 --> 00:01:09.560
but it's presumably
too metabolically costly

00:01:09.560 --> 00:01:12.040
to have it run at full tilt
all the time

00:01:12.040 --> 00:01:14.040
even when
we don't really need it.

00:01:14.040 --> 00:01:17.400
But ramping up DNA insults
with low dose radiation

00:01:17.400 --> 00:01:19.280
signals to the animal

00:01:19.280 --> 00:01:21.600
that they are in a DNA
destructive environment;

00:01:21.600 --> 00:01:26.680
so, their body starts ramping up
DNA repair to compensate.

00:01:26.680 --> 00:01:29.840
And a happy side effect of
all that extra DNA protection

00:01:30.360 --> 00:01:32.240
is a longer life.

00:01:32.240 --> 00:01:36.280
That which didn't kill them
made them stronger.

00:01:36.280 --> 00:01:38.720
Hormesis is not just
for insects.

00:01:38.720 --> 00:01:40.760
It may explain
the findings of the study

00:01:40.760 --> 00:01:43.200
"Low-dose radiation
from A-bombs

00:01:43.200 --> 00:01:46.600
elongated lifespan
and reduced cancer mortality

00:01:46.600 --> 00:01:50.320
relative to un-irradiated
individuals."

00:01:50.320 --> 00:01:54.600
The atomic bombs dropped
on Hiroshima and Nagasaki

00:01:54.600 --> 00:01:58.680
killed approximately
200,000 people instantaneously,

00:01:58.680 --> 00:02:01.120
and survivors exposed
to high levels of radiation

00:02:01.120 --> 00:02:04.880
suffered from high rates
of cancer and shortened lives.

00:02:04.880 --> 00:02:08.480
However, those exposed
to lower levels of radiation

00:02:08.480 --> 00:02:10.760
living farther
from the blast site

00:02:10.760 --> 00:02:13.640
appeared to end up
with lower cancer mortality

00:02:13.640 --> 00:02:16.720
and longer average lifespans.

00:02:16.720 --> 00:02:18.360
Exceptional medical services

00:02:18.360 --> 00:02:20.840
provided to
the surviving victims

00:02:20.840 --> 00:02:24.280
under the Law Concerning Relief
to Atomic Bomb Survivors

00:02:24.280 --> 00:02:26.920
may explain some
of the longevity benefit,

00:02:26.920 --> 00:02:29.760
but it also could have been
a hormetic effect.

00:02:30.600 --> 00:02:33.240
"Nothing in life
is to be feared,"

00:02:33.240 --> 00:02:36.120
Madame Curie,
who won the Nobel Prize

00:02:36.120 --> 00:02:38.680
for discovering radioactivity,
is quoted as saying,

00:02:38.680 --> 00:02:41.760
"it is only to be understood."

00:02:41.760 --> 00:02:44.000
Of course,
this is coming from a woman

00:02:44.000 --> 00:02:48.080
who died of bone marrow failure
from radiation exposure,

00:02:48.080 --> 00:02:52.640
such that her remains were
interred in a lead-lined coffin.

00:02:52.640 --> 00:02:57.280
Why would animals evolve to be
able to withstand radiation?

00:02:57.280 --> 00:02:59.520
Because we're bombarded
day and night

00:02:59.520 --> 00:03:01.880
by cosmic rays
from the universe.

00:03:01.880 --> 00:03:06.080
Our bodies are exposed to
about 20,000 hits of radiation

00:03:06.080 --> 00:03:07.800
every second.

00:03:07.800 --> 00:03:10.240
But what if we weren't?

00:03:10.240 --> 00:03:11.760
Scientists have found

00:03:11.760 --> 00:03:14.000
that single-celled organisms
like paramecia

00:03:14.000 --> 00:03:17.120
don't grow as well
in lead boxes,

00:03:17.120 --> 00:03:18.720
and the thicker the lead walls,

00:03:18.720 --> 00:03:20.920
the more their growth
is stunted.

00:03:20.920 --> 00:03:24.640
Human cells grown under
similarly shielded conditions

00:03:24.640 --> 00:03:28.600
show an increase in levels
of DNA damage and mutations.

00:03:28.600 --> 00:03:31.200
This suggests the natural
background radiation

00:03:31.200 --> 00:03:32.080
of the Earth

00:03:32.080 --> 00:03:36.600
has the hormetic benefit
of keeping our body on its toes.

00:03:36.600 --> 00:03:38.000
Even a foot (0.3048 m) of lead

00:03:38.000 --> 00:03:40.520
only blocks about
a third of cosmic rays.

00:03:40.520 --> 00:03:42.640
To really see
what life would be like

00:03:42.640 --> 00:03:44.800
without constant bombardment,

00:03:44.800 --> 00:03:47.200
scientists descended
more than a mile (1.6 km)

00:03:47.200 --> 00:03:50.440
down into the Earth
into SNOLAB,

00:03:50.440 --> 00:03:52.520
the Sudbury Neutrino
Observatory,

00:03:52.520 --> 00:03:55.760
set at the bottom
of a nickel mine in Canada.

00:03:55.760 --> 00:03:57.680
Contrary to expectations,

00:03:57.680 --> 00:04:00.720
fish raised deep underground
grew bigger and heavier

00:04:00.720 --> 00:04:02.640
than those raised
on the surface.

00:04:02.640 --> 00:04:06.600
The researchers suggested the
silencing of cosmic radiation

00:04:06.600 --> 00:04:09.000
may have been offset
by increased radiation

00:04:09.000 --> 00:04:12.360
from radon gas
trapped in the mine.

00:04:12.360 --> 00:04:15.880
Bottom line: we don't know
enough about low-level radiation

00:04:15.880 --> 00:04:17.800
to exploit any hormetic effects

00:04:17.800 --> 00:04:21.200
without potentially being
exposed to unacceptable risks.

00:04:21.200 --> 00:04:25.320
Thankfully, there are salutary
ways to harness hormesis

00:04:25.320 --> 00:04:29.600
for health and longevity.

